A license notice is never a header, and it says nothing about the rule below it either: CSS takes the comment directly above a rule as its leading annotation, but not a comment the header search passed over.
`only-license.css` has no header, and `.a` starts at its own line; in `license-then-header.css` the header comes after the license, and `.b` starts at the comment directly above it.
== args
input/only-license.css
input/license-then-header.css
== file input/only-license.css
/* Copyright 2024 Acme */
.a { color: red }
== file input/license-then-header.css
/* Copyright 2024 Acme */
/* Theme colors. */

/* The brand color. */
.b { color: blue }
== stdout
input/only-license.css (2 lines)
[L2-L2] .a

input/license-then-header.css (5 lines)
Theme colors.
[L4-L5] .b
== stderr
== exit 0
